{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character","id":762438,"title":"Help me brainstorm this character","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-10T11:09:15-08:00","id":762438,"title":"Help me brainstorm this character","content":"Essentially what it says above. I'm still fleshing this character out.<br /> <br /> The basic concept of the character is that he's this guy who in life was just a really nice guy. His parents always instilled in him the importance of doing the right thing, so he spent all his time doing charity work, and political activism, and just trying to make the world a better place. Then in a twist of fate, he got turned. I'll spare you all the details, unless anyone really wants them, but essentially he woke up to a note from his sire that said &quot;Hey, you're a vampire now. Also vampires are real. I can't really help you figure this shit out because of reasons, but here are all the basic rules (Both the traditions and the rules of how vampires work). Also, I can't tell you where to find the prince because reasons, and he'll probably kill you for not presenting yourself to him, so try not to draw attention to yourself.<br /> <br /> So this guy who all he wants to do is just do the right thing and be helpful and kind has woken up to find that he's now this creature that, by its nature, needs to prey on others in order to survive. So he's utterly unable, on a moral level, to feed on other humans because he can't bring himself to do it. And even when he tried to feed on animals, he couldn't bring himself to do that, because in his mind, they're completely innocent and while he was able to eat meat in life, it was another thing when he had to hunt down these actual creatures and force himself on them.<br /> <br /> What he found he was able to do to justify this was that he couldn't bring himself to feed on innocent people, but non-innocent people? That was a slightly different prospect. He still didn't like it, but he could justify it enough that he could bring himself to do it. Of course, vampires aren't so tough that they can get into fights with humans and win without using their special powers. So he had to violate the masquerade. And thus draw attention to himself. To mitigate this, he's adopted a disguise and an alternate identity, so that the vampire powers that be are forced to chase after a specter, and he can hide himself away otherwise.<br /> <br /> Essentially, through a series of accidents and natural logical leaps, this mild-mannered, well-meaning guy has become Vampire-Batman.<br /> <br /> At first, it wasn't too bad. Vampires occasionally have to make use of their disciplines to feed and the authorities that be (The setting is this kind of amalgam of Requiem and Masquerade, where it's the requiem clans, but with the Camarilla and Sabbat and Caine and all that good stuff) are used to dealing with it. But over the past years, more and more reports have been filtering in of a hooded figure hiding behind a mask, defending the weak with inhuman powers. Human authorities have been writing it off as local superstition, but the Camarilla knows better. And our story is opening right as they're getting ready to crack down.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Onto the advice I need.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> The biggest thing is that I'm still torn on is a clan for this guy. I have two immediate inklings<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1. Nosferatu<br /> <br /> Pros: The Nos really play well to the fact that this guy has been transformed into a monster against his will, and from a character perspective it makes a lot of sense to give him a curse like that for him to rail against. I like the image of this guy still trying to be kind and generous to the people around him and being unable because they're all reacting to him with sheer terror. From a mechanical perspective, he gets the 2 disciplines I know I'm going to need to rely on, Vigor and Obfuscate, as clan disciplines. Nightmare also works great with the concept as something he can unleash against the baddies beyond just wailing on them.<br /> <br /> Cons: This might be petty, but I really like the image of the guy with the hood and the mask and why would he even need the mask if his actual face is horrifying and monstrous looking. At that point he doesn't have an identity that he needs to hide. He can't go outside anyway. He may as well just walk around in jeans and a t-shirt. I know in requiem Nosferatu don't have to be ugly, and they just have this &quot;menacing aura&quot; but eh? I wouldn't fault another player for it, but for me it feels like a cop-out to make a Nosferatu and not fuck up his face at least a little bit. They're the ugly vampires, damn it. They're the Anti-Rice! On a mechanical note, I only need the one dot of obfuscate, and it's a generic discipline so I can take the one dot at character creation and not deal with it anymore. And if all I need is vigor at that point, I may was well get a clan or a bloodline that'd give it to me and get some other disciplines I'd like to fill out more. I also don't know how effective Nightmare really is in play. Does anyone know how good a discipline it is in practice? (Post blood and smoke)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 2. Daeva<br /> <br /> Pros: Essentially that he doesn't have to deal with the cons of being a Nosferatu, and still has vigor. I also know from experience what a great discipline majesty is and it seems like it would be all-around more useful. Also the idea of dressing up in a costume is ridiculous and flashy enough that it seems like the kind of thing a Daeva would do. I'm also planning on making this guy as much a social character as he is a fighter, to represent his human life in addition to the skills he's had to pick up to survive, and that works a bit more with a Daeva, who's a lot better equipped to be a social character.<br /> <br /> Cons: Doesn't have all the flavor that comes with Nos mixing in with his character. At least no more than any other generic vampire. Also planning on making this guy more brute strength than grace and speed which doesn't totally gel with my concept of a Daeva.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Nosferatu seems like the better fit overall, but there's enough there making me hesitant that I'm tempted to go with Daeva, which I have more experience playing with.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also not sure on what would be some good merits for him. I put down a few dots of fighting style: martial arts and the obligatory dot in resources, but beyond that I'm not sure what would really be good for the concept.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:42:32-08:00","id":762570,"title":"","content":"<br /> The embrace sound like a gangrel sire and abandon.<br /> Daeve have speed and Strength. Not having obfuscate could help with mask issue. <br /> <br /> Are you using Requiem 1 or 2?<br /> Have you looked at Beast that hunts the Blood? Requiems Nos clan book?<br /> <br /> No Mekhet?<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:21:07-08:00","id":762595,"title":"","content":"Requiem 2. Mekhet just doesn't jive with me. Both their bonuses are to mental attributes which I've kind of accepted as this guy's weakest point. Like he's a nice kid, but he's about as sharp as a bowling ball. I have no idea what beast that hunts the blood is and I don't have the Nos clan book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T14:23:35-08:00","id":762597,"title":"","content":"Also, it wasn't quite a case of sire and abandon. Without getting too into it, he saw a confrontation going down, stuck his nose into it to try to help get a peaceful resolution, and got stabbed for his troubles. The guy he was trying to help turned out to be a vampire, and basically whatever decency was left in his heart got stirred when he saw this and he decided to save him. And between ghouling or embracing him, the embrace seemed like the less shitty way to do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T15:40:59-08:00","id":762663,"title":"","content":"Nosferatu have a thing for masks. You can do the mask thing with a Nos despite the already monstrous appearance. In fact there's a Merit in the Nos ClanBook called Unyielding Mask that grants bonuses to skills and resisting mental and social disciplines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><b>I</b>'m <b>S</b>o <b>M</b>eta <b>E</b>ven <b>T</b>his <b>A</b>cronym</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/195-thorbes","name":"Thorbes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar195_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2982"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T18:59:32-08:00","id":762755,"title":"","content":"True, although if I do go with a Nos, I wouldn't want to permanently hide his appearance. Unyielding masks are like welded to the guy's face.<br /> <br /> What I just thought of is to make his appearance frightening, but not monstrous. Like he doesn't look like Count Orlok, so much as his face is made of features that don't quite mesh with each other. Like give him the classic pale, clammy skin and yellow pupils, but his head is still human shaped. But then there are little details that are just wrong like his eyes are a little too big. His fangs only retract so far as to fit into his mouth and they're still visible when he opens it. The end result is that he's very disconcerting to look at, but it's less terrifying monster and more uncanny valley. Kinda like those ladies who got cosmetic surgery to look like Barbie Dolls. So as long as no one gets a really good look at him, he can still kinda pass for human. He just looks like a human who's done a lot of body modification to himself and is probably some kind of weirdo you should stay away from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T00:26:48-08:00","id":762890,"title":"","content":"This is a personal choice but I really like making Nosferatu (as NPCs) that aren't that ugly but are disturbing in more subtle ways. If you wanted to be a Nos that was still reasonably good looking here are some ideas.<br /> <br /> His eyes are just dead, always. Its not that they just don't show emotion, its like staring into the inanimate eyes of corpse. Good luck making eye contact. Otherwise he looks normal.<br /> <br /> His skin is constantly bruising giving him a permanent post-bar room fight or the drawn out junkie look.<br /> <br /> He consistently leaks some drops of blood from his eyes and nose, especially during social scenarios. <br /> <br /> He has a permanent, aggressive air of menace about him. People get the impression he could flip and turn violent at any point, regardless of what he actually feels. This would be an interesting contrast to his more heroic actions.<br /> <br /> If I can think of some more later I'll come back with some.<br /> Some other ideas, the guys has a weird smell about him or he has an-off putting voice. Anything that makes him slightly off.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1161-gravitas-man","name":"Gravitas Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T02:40:16-08:00","id":762956,"title":"","content":"Firstly their are plentiful reasons to go nos mask obbs, as someone with Obfuscate has no need of a mask he might expect the powers that be to overlook him if he has it. Second it would be too easy for a Deave to talk people into agreeing to give him blood so I would avoid that clan.<br /> All in all a good concept but remember that being in a bloodline would mean your sire giving you another point of blood (level one bloodbond) and give a way to narrow down who he is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4714-live-bait","name":"Live Bait","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T08:10:02-08:00","id":763122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=762595#post762595\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Requiem 2. Mekhet just doesn't jive with me. Both their bonuses are to mental attributes which I've kind of accepted as this guy's weakest point. Like he's a nice kid, but he's about as sharp as a bowling ball. <b>I have no idea what beast that hunts the blood is and I don't have the Nos clan book</b></div> </div> </div> </div>They are one in the same.<br /> There is an alternate take on their weakness in it.<br /> Pick two skills. One gets a bonus the other get a social related minus, both increases with blood potency.<br /> They are meant to be related and reflect something makes him strange. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If you want By Night Studios to release new LARP RULES for NWoD,<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/313137-open-letter-to-by-night-studios\" target=\"_blank\">like this post</a>.<br /> <br /> <img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=62\" data-tempid=\"temp_62_1418088885567_853\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/594-chattnos","name":"Chattnos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar594_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"879"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T18:22:06-08:00","id":763638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chattnos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=762570#post762570\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Mekhet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seconded. Mekhet is a suitable fit and they too have obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Also why so violent?? Violence is completely unnecessary and seems to strongly run counter to your character. Unless he has a blood potency that requires human blood consumption he should feed from animals, and animals can be purchased. With help, from a trusted retainer possibly ghouled for the health benefits, a brood mate or his sire they can easily manage a large animal into a pen for bloodletting. It sounds like your character having a background in philanthropy must be a moneyed individual. A lovely country house with a few grazing animals is a perfect place to keep fed. Heck if your character is disease free the meat could be butchered and donated to feed the hungry.<br /> <br /> If blood potency is too high to feed on animals, well then it'd be better off to pay vampires more capable of easily subduing people who easily disappear/meet your ethical requirements than to assume you'll have the ability to do so without fatal to you consequences. Don't play a suicidal character, all that does is punish game continuity by the other players going easy on you when they should ruthlessly get rid of you, or promote ruthless play that is hostile to new players, both of which are bad.<br /> <br /> Vigor should be completely useless to the type of character you described.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-11-2015, 09:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T19:14:35-08:00","id":763667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=763638#post763638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seconded. Mekhet is a suitable fit and they too have obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Also why so violent?? Violence is completely unnecessary and seems to strongly run counter to your character. Unless he has a blood potency that requires human blood consumption he should feed from animals, and animals can be purchased. With help, from a trusted retainer possibly ghouled for the health benefits, a brood mate or his sire they can easily manage a large animal into a pen for bloodletting. It sounds like your character having a background in philanthropy must be a moneyed individual. A lovely country house with a few grazing animals is a perfect place to keep fed. Heck if your character is disease free the meat could be butchered and donated to feed the hungry.<br /> <br /> If blood potency is too high to feed on animals, well then it'd be better off to pay vampires more capable of easily subduing people who easily disappear/meet your ethical requirements than to assume you'll have the ability to do so without fatal to you consequences. Don't play a suicidal character, all that does is punish game continuity by the other players going easy on you when they should ruthlessly get rid of you, or promote ruthless play that is hostile to new players, both of which are bad.<br /> <br /> Vigor should be completely useless to the type of character you described.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, he's unwilling to feed from animals because he feels just as guilty feeding from them as he does from innocent people. As far as he's concerned, they didn't do anything wrong to merit that kind of violation. To him, someone committing a violent crime has at least done something to merit being attacked by a creature of the night.<br /> <br /> His strong moral beliefs are the same reason he wouldn't ghoul somebody. Hell, I don't know if the process of ghouling someone would even be something he knew. And like I said, his sire isn't in the picture and has done everything in his or her power to keep him out of Vampire society out of self-preservation. When the story begins, he isn't even going to know any other vampires, not even the other players.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, he wasn't a philanthropist. He was a charity <i>worker. </i>He volunteered his time and his energy at soup kitchens, political rallies, etc. As far as money goes, he didn't have a pot to piss in or a window to throw it out of. He went down to the local shelter and made sandwiches all day, or something like that. His 9-5 job was working retail.<br /> <br /> He's not a violent person by nature. That's kinda the point. He's a peaceful person being thrust into circumstances where he's going to have to become increasingly dependent on violence to survive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6337,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","user":"someguywithakatana","date":". 11-11-2015, 10:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:54:33-08:00","id":764522,"title":"","content":"I apologize but what you are saying just doesn't make any sense. While alive did he eat the flesh of criminals because animals didn't deserve to be cut into pieces? The extreme you are suggesting is criminally insane if it were a real person. A person with a &quot;strong moral belief&quot; doesn't eat people if he doesn't believe he has to, no matter what.<br /> <br /> Also your story has several obstacles. First is how a working stiff who wouldn't believe in vampires would assume he's a creature of the night after waking up without a bite mark after an attack. Obviously without some extreme circumstances, he wouldn't.<br /> <br /> Did he call the police or seek medical aid? How would that work out for him?<br /> <br /> Assuming he gets through that, said character is likely to die from his first sunrise.<br /> <br /> If he's an apartment dweller, his screams from being set on fire by the sun will not go unnoticed by his neighbors. If he is a private home owner (in this economy, without room mates or a spouses second income?? That would be Fantasy, not modern horror genre) then he might survive the scramble to a closet or bathroom.<br /> <br /> Why would the character feed in the first place? Obviously he wouldn't choose to, he would feel extremely hungry and then be overtaken in a hunger frenzy when exposed to stimuli. That's a mess and potentially public/semi-public scene.<br /> <br /> Really a vampire without a sire in the environment of fundamental disbelief in the supernatural will Frenzy. In the modern day urban dense population a irrational unplanned violent outburst is both a site of an orgy of evidence, and likely reported in most cities. I live in Portland Oregon, we had 14 murders in 2013. A vampire like the one you are describing would immediately draw the attention of the local vampires through their contacts in authorizes, hospitals, and media or heck even if one vampire just listened to the police scanner. The mehket of the area would be able to use their powers to investigate to see the supernatural cause of the murder, and with only 14 murders in a year they could research each murder, and they'd find you in less than a week, assuming the mages/werewolves/hunters didn't find you first.<br /> <br /> You must remember your character doesn't live in a vacuum, and plot immunity of unlikely contrivances you grant them in your mind as you make their back story just makes them ill-suited to exist in the actual game world.<br /> <br /> I would recommend scrapping your concept because it is based on a flawed premise that doesn't work because it is inconsistent to what you say the character is (ie not internally consistent) and inconsistent with the setting and how it works.<br /> <br /> I think I know what you are looking for, (a character with a moral struggle) but having no sire is a death sentence, or a sure way to make a character that the other monsters in your game would just put down (if they played their characters correctly). Don't be that guy.<br /> <br /> Have a sire, have attachments to the setting, make a character that eats only animals and won't resort to the stuff you are talking about until either your play experience shakes the character's naivete or his blood potency rises in play and he is left no other choice. It is better for your character, the story, your fellow players and the storyteller. Don't skip the parts of the story that are truly interesting, the part where the character didn't eat people because of his morals, and the part where he began to and the reasons why.<br /> <br /> Murder-hobos, (which a vampire with retail experience on his resume and no family, friends or sire is) are lame. Don't be a murder-hobo.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 11-13-2015, 01:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T17:48:21-08:00","id":764570,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=763667#post763667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, he's unwilling to feed from animals because he feels just as guilty feeding from them as he does from innocent people. As far as he's concerned, they didn't do anything wrong to merit that kind of violation. To him, someone committing a violent crime has at least done something to merit being attacked by a creature of the night.<br /> <br /> His strong moral beliefs are the same reason he wouldn't ghoul somebody. Hell, I don't know if the process of ghouling someone would even be something he knew. And like I said, his sire isn't in the picture and has done everything in his or her power to keep him out of Vampire society out of self-preservation. When the story begins, he isn't even going to know any other vampires, not even the other players.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Also, he wasn't a philanthropist. He was a charity <i>worker. </i>He volunteered his time and his energy at soup kitchens, political rallies, etc. As far as money goes, he didn't have a pot to piss in or a window to throw it out of. He went down to the local shelter and made sandwiches all day, or something like that. His 9-5 job was working retail.<br /> <br /> He's not a violent person by nature. That's kinda the point. He's a peaceful person being thrust into circumstances where he's going to have to become increasingly dependent on violence to survive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just saw this, but I feel like pointing out that <i>A Hunger Like Fire </i>by Greg Stolze is a Vampire: The Requiem novel which deals with this exact issue at one point in the book, and shows some of the consequences that arise from going after people you think &quot;deserve it.&quot;<br /> <br /> It can make for great dramatic play, and your <i>CHARACTER </i>almost certainly won't see how this doesn't end well, but as a player, you should definitely keep in mind that it's a dangerous practice to feed on people you have contempt for.<br /> <br /> Kindred feeding is not an exact science, and if you hate someone for something they've done and it makes you angry while you're feeding, you are really at a fair risk of draining them without realizing what you're doing and frenzying and killing them. Ironically, feeding on people who <i>don't </i>deserve it is probably easier, because you're motivated to <i>not </i>just drain them dry.<br /> <br /> Mechanically, your character will also suffer breaking points for assaulting these people while feeding. Violence like that is dehumanizing. You might find the character's Humanity descending as a consequence of his practices, which might even start to negate the reason he fed that way in the first place.<br /> <br /> If this is coming across like a warning, please let me clarify: This is <i>awesome</i>. This is the stuff Requiem is made to be about. Examining how your character engages with this idea and the pitfalls of it is perfectly suited to Requiem. That's a cool direction to take your character in.<br /> <br /> Also, you should read <i>A Hunger Like Fire</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T16:36:34-08:00","id":765213,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=764522#post764522\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I apologize but what you are saying just doesn't make any sense. While alive did he eat the flesh of criminals because animals didn't deserve to be cut into pieces? The extreme you are suggesting is criminally insane if it were a real person. A person with a &quot;strong moral belief&quot; doesn't eat people if he doesn't believe he has to, no matter what.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was saying the character ate ANIMALS while he was alive. You know, like hamburgers and such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T17:13:29-08:00","id":765237,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765213#post765213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was saying the character ate ANIMALS while he was alive. You know, like hamburgers and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was exactly the point I was making. Eating bad people as a vampire while eating animals is possible because &quot;he's unwilling to feed from animals because he feels just as guilty feeding from them as he does from innocent people&quot; is insane. It is exactly like while alive eating ground-up criminals instead of beef in your hamburgers, for &quot;strong moral belief&quot; reasons. It makes no sense, is internally inconsistent and is extreme to the point of being criminally insane.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T17:28:09-08:00","id":765245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mangle77</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765213#post765213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was saying the character ate ANIMALS while he was alive. You know, like hamburgers and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hence the cognitive dissonance Pale_Crusader is pointing out with this character concept. The proposed character gave no thought to the number of animals slaughtered to feed him when he was alive because he never had to actually hunt and kill them. But now he can't bring himself to visit a slaughterhouse or kill an animal to save himself, however he'll blithely hunt and murder suspected criminals because they deserve to die. Was cannibalism acceptable behavior to the character when he was alive? Did the character believe everyone accused of a crime should die? There is no indication of such beliefs being espoused in the proposal.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T17:32:42-08:00","id":765246,"title":"","content":"I agree. Scrap the no eating animals thing would be my suggestion, because it's bananas. There are less animals in general to feed from in the city, and there are other natural ways to make the progression to feeding on the guilty from there. The only way it makes sense for him to hate feeding on animals in Undeath and not in Life is if he has a sort of self-hatred thing going on or finds the process of drinking blood disgusting or distasteful. In which case one would imagine that would still extend to feeding on the guilty.<br /> <br /> The guy is clearly a Nosferatu in my mind. Covenant can vary, but Carthian would make sense to me, or none at all. Remember, Nosferatu thrive on fear, if you're making a Batman that's the way to go. And as has already been mentioned, they don't have to be hideous, just unsettling. The Unyielding Mask merit is a fantastic choice if you want to go that route.<br /> <br /> Daeva wouldn't make sense for a character who lurks in the shadows and who has so much concern with right and wrong over hedonistic pleasure. Certainly Majesty doesn't fit the guy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 11-13-2015, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T18:36:47-08:00","id":765276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That was exactly the point I was making. Eating bad people as a vampire while eating animals is possible because &quot;he's unwilling to feed from animals because he feels just as guilty feeding from them as he does from innocent people&quot; is insane. It is exactly like while alive eating ground-up criminals instead of beef in your hamburgers, for &quot;strong moral belief&quot; reasons. It makes no sense, is internally inconsistent and is extreme to the point of being criminally insane. </div> </div> </div>The idea, as I understood it, was that he hates feeding on the innocent. I know<i> I </i>wouldn't feel comfortable having to kill a cow, but I can still eat meat. Causing severe harm to some rapist or mugger in an alley? Maybe wouldn't bother me as much.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":6138,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","user":"Mangle77","date":". 11-13-2015, 09:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T08:53:30-08:00","id":765582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765246#post765246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Daeva wouldn't make sense for a character who lurks in the shadows and who has so much concern with right and wrong over hedonistic pleasure. Certainly Majesty doesn't fit the guy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being a Daeva does not forever condemn you to hedonism, and the conflict between playing someone who can make people want them and can walk all over those people while really NOT wanting to do that could be interesting.<br /> <br /> Plus, it's not as if you get your pick of Vampires coming to embrace you. The player may decide their character's clan, but the character doesn't, not really.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T09:39:57-08:00","id":765613,"title":"","content":"Oh, I know this. But three counterpoints.<br /> <br /> Yes, it doesn't condemn you to a life of wanton hedonism, but that is the fantasy of the Daeva. If not hedonism, then at least aestheticism. As a creator why create a Daeva that doesn't embrace the fantasy? Unless, as you said you are specifically trying to subvert that fantasy as part of your character idea. Which he very well could be.<br /> <br /> And in game, you are less likely to be turned by a Daeva if you yourself aren't the kind of person a Daeva would be inclined to turn. Not that it's likely for any clan, but it seems especially unlikely that a Daeva would turn this charity worker for no reason. And consider that being made a Daeva does influence both your Beast and your Curse. It's not just a club you get sworn into. Daeva's tend toward hedonism for a reason.<br /> <br /> Further, the letter less florid/focused on the beauty of vampirism than I'd expect from a Daeva. Yes, I'm stereotyping but that helps when deciding where a character best fits, and there's nothing that suggests Daeva to me. Lust is their defining trait.<br /> <br /> The only real angle I see is as you said, a Daeva in denial, trying to square his lust with his old morals. Horrified at how much he loves to feed and staunchly refusing to, except he can't stop himself. So he finds a way by perverting it as some way to mete out justice. The whole &quot;I can't do it to animals&quot; thing is an obvious lie, he just can't stomach ground chuck when he's had a taste of filet mignon.<br /> <br /> Nosferatu is a better fit (or Gangrel), as is, in my eyes, any clan. Daeva would be the last choice for this character except where clan disciplines are concerned. I was just brainstorming like the OP asked. My opinion is another grain of salt to take as you please. I was, like many others, more confused by the not feeding on animals thing than clan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 11-14-2015, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T11:01:53-08:00","id":765658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765613#post765613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I know this. But three counterpoints.<br /> <br /> Yes, it doesn't condemn you to a life of wanton hedonism, but that is the fantasy of the Daeva. If not hedonism, then at least aestheticism. As a creator why create a Daeva that doesn't embrace the fantasy? Unless, as you said you are specifically trying to subvert that fantasy as part of your character idea. Which he very well could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Social workers often have a position of advantage over the people they work with. Daeva often have signiciant power over the mortals they interact with. The fantasy of a Daeva is a social worker's worst nightmare and intensely traumatizing, and it's a remarkably <i>easy </i>power to use to make your Requiem easier. Nevermind the idea of subverting the archetype, there's a rich playground of power differentials and coerced behavior and misguided 'help' to be had in playing a Daeva. They disrupt the lives around them. That's a lot of material to work with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765613#post765613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in game, you are less likely to be turned by a Daeva if you yourself aren't the kind of person a Daeva would be inclined to turn. Not that it's likely for any clan, but it seems especially unlikely that a Daeva would turn this charity worker for no reason. And consider that being made a Daeva does influence both your Beast and your Curse. It's not just a club you get sworn into. Daeva's tend toward hedonism for a reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we want to really take a look at Daeva in 2e, they're arguably the least likely clan to have a &quot;type&quot; precisely because their Curse is not picky about who they're obsessed with, and that obsession seems like one of the ways that Daeva might Embrace. (If you look at the fiction that inspires Daeva, you'll see that behavior of obsession and possession replay itself multiple times.<br /> <br /> If you look at the way the mechanics reinforce the nature of the Daeva, it's that it gives them a tool that's easy to use to help solve problems (Majesty and Awe), it can make you innately better at manipulating people or moving fast, and it lends itself to becoming obsessed with the mortals you feed on. <br /> <br /> The idea of their hedonism is really more of a 1e thing. They're not &quot;the ones who host debauched parties&quot; they're &quot;the ones you love&quot; and you might observe that all the talk of sex goddesses isn't the talk of sex seeking for self pleasure. It's talking about it through the medium of divinity and worship. The thematics of the Daeva in 2nd edition aren't of hedonism, they're about worship, power over others, love and obsession, and pleasure derived through those things.<br /> <br /> I think if you're looking specifically for hedonism within this set, I'd either make it a part of the character's concept, their immediate Kindred lineage, or part of their Bloodline identity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765613#post765613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Further, the letter less florid/focused on the beauty of vampirism than I'd expect from a Daeva. Yes, I'm stereotyping but that helps when deciding where a character best fits, and there's nothing that suggests Daeva to me. Lust is their defining trait.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's better articulated as extreme &quot;want&quot;, which a character obsessed with trying to maintain his own morality might be appropriate, but I can't do much to help you there if you're stereotyping like that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765613#post765613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only real angle I see is as you said, a Daeva in denial, trying to square his lust with his old morals. Horrified at how much he loves to feed and staunchly refusing to, except he can't stop himself. So he finds a way by perverting it as some way to mete out justice. The whole &quot;I can't do it to animals&quot; thing is an obvious lie, he just can't stomach ground chuck when he's had a taste of filet mignon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget about the Curse. Being obsessed with mortals, possibly with an idea in mind that you can fix them (a la a social worker) could lead to a lot of cool drama. The social worker might think it's all about them, but he might have to swallow the bitter pill once he's forced to realize what his almost accidental Majesty-persuasion has done to their friend's ability to make independent choices, or focus on themselves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amravanti</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765613#post765613\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nosferatu is a better fit (or Gangrel), as is, in my eyes, any clan. Daeva would be the last choice for this character except where clan disciplines are concerned. I was just brainstorming like the OP asked. My opinion is another grain of salt to take as you please. I was, like many others, more confused by the not feeding on animals thing than clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nosferatu are also a really good fit too in my opinion, because the &quot;loneliness&quot; has a lot of material to play with in the idea of a person who had such a people-oriented job. What do you do when your entire life was based around other people coming to you, with you helping them, with them being grateful for your help, and now they don't want to be around you?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying a Daeva is the perfect fit above all, just that we needn't be overly proscriptive and that there's a lot of stuff to play with there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T13:16:21-08:00","id":766489,"title":"","content":"I confess I didn't pick up on the tone change for Daeva in 2e. I'm still familiarizing myself with the changes. Even with that in mind, it feels like one of the choices that synergises the least with the character concept, though I will accept that it is not an entirely inscrutable/confusing choice. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the clan choice was a minor objection and I did not mean to get into an argument about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T00:22:40-08:00","id":766897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Pale_Crusader</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=765237#post765237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That was exactly the point I was making. Eating bad people as a vampire while eating animals is possible because &quot;he's unwilling to feed from animals because he feels just as guilty feeding from them as he does from innocent people&quot; is insane. It is exactly like while alive eating ground-up criminals instead of beef in your hamburgers, for &quot;strong moral belief&quot; reasons. It makes no sense, is internally inconsistent and is extreme to the point of being criminally insane.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Going to the store, buying some meat, cooking it.<br /> <br /> 2. Finding a live animal, chasing it down, biting into it and sucking its blood dry as it kicks and screams to get away.<br /> <br /> There is a difference between these two actions. Not morally, perhaps, but psychologically","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6337-someguywithakatana","name":"someguywithakatana","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-16T07:18:12-08:00","id":767049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>someguywithakatana</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/762438-help-me-brainstorm-this-character?p=766897#post766897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Going to the store, buying some meat, cooking it.<br /> <br /> 2. Finding a live animal, chasing it down, biting into it and sucking its blood dry as it kicks and screams to get away.<br /> <br /> There is a difference between these two actions. Not morally, perhaps, but psychologically</div> </div> </div> </div>You forgot an item, the one that gives me pause.<br /> <br /> 3. Finding a human (who happens to have commited a crime), hunting them down, biting into them and sucking their blood dry until they fall limp onto the floor of some back alleyway and their eyes close forever.<br /> <br /> If you're talking about morality then there's no difference between 1 and 2, and 2 is not worse than 3. If you're talking about psychology then 2 is also not worse than 3. Of course both those previous statements come with a caveat: Unless you're a crazy person. <br /> <br /> If you're so moral that you are devastated at the thought of catching and drinking an 'innocent' rat (you want to talk about guilty animals) then surely you're moral enough to realize that these criminals have families, children, and that humans can be rehabilitated, that humans sometimes make mistakes/bad life choices, and that humans are sometimes driven to do things they never thought themselves capable of if they have no other choice. And I mean, unless he's going after only pedophiles, rapists and unrepentant murderers (and even then) I don't know how long that justification would hold up for a sane person. There's a reason Batman isn't the Punisher, and there's a reason The Punisher is also okay with killing a squirrel if he needs to eat one night (I am making assumptions about the Punisher's personality).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}